    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          2
        ],
        "content": "## Intake new client enquiries from Gmail with Claude into Clio and DocuSign\n\nLaw firms and professional practices that reply to enquiries a day late and re-key them into the practice system.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: An email to the intake address, a website form submission, or a phone note typed into the shared inbox starts intake for that enquiry.\n1. Receive the enquiry\n2. Classify the matter\n3. Extract the conflict-check facts\n4. Run the conflict check\n5. Acknowledge\n6. Draft the next document\n7. Approve\n8. Open the matter\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items; the write-back waits for an approval.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus Clio / PracticePanther, Gmail / Outlook, DocuSign / PandaDoc.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nDefine the practice areas and the conflict-check questions in the Config node; swap Clio for PracticePanther.\nGuardrail to keep: Nothing is sent to an enquirer except the acknowledgement until a person approves; no advice or fee is ever quoted automatically.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/client-intake-automation/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
